Falsifies `inter_process_communication::notification::verification::a_waiter_is_woken_before_the_bound_receiver`.

The defect: rule 2 before rule 1, so a signal goes to the bound receiver while a thread waits on
the notification itself. Both deliveries are "a wake", which is why the order is easy to swap.

Expected to fail: the `Signal::ToBound(_) => assert!(!had_waiter && bound)` arm, with a waiter
seeded and `bound` true.

